WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.869
Can a court give a Governor

2
00:00:01.869 --> 00:00:03.727
a deadline to decide on a bill?

3
00:00:04.277 --> 00:00:07.093
Article 200 gives the Governor options:

4
00:00:07.243 --> 00:00:08.865
assent, withhold assent,

5
00:00:08.965 --> 00:00:10.397
or reserve the bill for the

6
00:00:10.397 --> 00:00:10.927
President.

7
00:00:11.327 --> 00:00:13.205
It sets no fixed time limit.

8
00:00:13.705 --> 00:00:15.875
In April 2025, a two-judge

9
00:00:15.875 --> 00:00:17.545
bench set timelines,

10
00:00:17.665 --> 00:00:19.272
and treated ten Tamil Nadu

11
00:00:19.272 --> 00:00:21.249
bills as having received assent.

12
00:00:21.699 --> 00:00:23.445
The President then sought

13
00:00:23.445 --> 00:00:25.191
the Court's opinion under

14
00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:26.029
Article 143.

15
00:00:26.479 --> 00:00:30.085
In November 2025, five judges advised:

16
00:00:30.235 --> 00:00:32.048
courts cannot fix timelines,

17
00:00:32.168 --> 00:00:33.939
and there is no deemed assent.

18
00:00:34.389 --> 00:00:35.856
But a Governor cannot sit

19
00:00:35.856 --> 00:00:37.205
on a bill indefinitely.

20
00:00:37.405 --> 00:00:38.924
For prolonged inaction, a

21
00:00:38.924 --> 00:00:40.626
court may direct a decision.

22
00:00:41.126 --> 00:00:42.513
No fixed clock.

23
00:00:42.813 --> 00:00:44.306
But no endless wait.

24
00:00:44.856 --> 00:00:45.795
Your turn.

25
00:00:46.095 --> 00:00:47.460
Which Article covers the

26
00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:48.996
Governor's assent to bills?
